# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ResolveAI - root .gitignore
#
# SECURITY NOTE: the entries under "Environment / secrets" deliberately ignore
# .env.example as well as the real .env files. The root .env.example previously
# contained live credentials; ignoring the whole family guarantees no env file
# can ever be staged, even if a real secret is pasted back into a template.
#
# TRADE-OFF: because .env.example is ignored, sanitized templates are NOT
# committed. A new deployer will not receive them from the repository and must
# be given the variable list out-of-band. If you would rather ship the sanitized
# templates, delete the ".env.example" line below and instead rely on the
# placeholders being real placeholders.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Environment / secrets -------------------------------------------------
# Real environment files (any directory, including backend/.env)
.env
.env.*
# Sanitized templates - intentionally not tracked, see note above
.env.example

# --- Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pypackages__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Next.js build output --------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.vercel/

# --- Generic build output --------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/

# --- Python bytecode / caches ---------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Test / coverage output ------------------------------------------------
coverage/
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# --- Evaluator generated output (scenarios live in version control) --------
backend/evaluation/integration/results/

# --- OS / editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
